{% doc %}
  Renders one accessible accordion row (native `<details>/<summary>`, no JS
  needed for open/close state) for the Montibello PDP's information stack,
  rendered inline as part of the right column in montibello-product-main.liquid
  (see that file for why). Keyboard-operable and exposes expanded/collapsed
  state natively via the `details` element. Closed by default (no `open`
  attribute). Caller is responsible for checking the underlying metafield is
  present before rendering — this snippet does not hide itself.

  LUXLIGHT TRUE VISUAL PARITY PASS: added `icon_source`. When 'official' the
  left icon and the right disclosure marker render via
  `montibello-luxlight-icon` (the real Montibello icon assets, reproduced
  from the official PDP's own SVG files — see that snippet's doc comment)
  instead of this theme's generic `snippets/icon.liquid` line-icon set. Any
  other value (including omitted) keeps the previous theme-icon behavior
  untouched — this is what keeps HOP/UNDER, which pass no `icon_source`,
  completely unaffected by this pass, per the explicit "ONLY THE 8 LUXLIGHT
  PDPs" scope limit.

  SMOOTH EXPANSION (Part 3 of the parity pass): native `<details>` has no
  built-in open/close transition — it snaps instantly. A small amount of JS
  (no framework, ~30 lines, scoped to `.montibello-pdp-accordion-item`
  elements only) intercepts the toggle, measures the content's natural
  height, and animates `max-height`/`opacity` over 280ms ease before
  actually toggling the `open` attribute (so screen readers/keyboard users
  still get correct native semantics throughout). `prefers-reduced-motion`
  is respected by skipping straight to the native instant toggle.

  @param {string} label - the closed-state row label, e.g. "Cómo usar"
  @param {string} content - pre-rendered HTML/rich text content to reveal
  @param {string} icon - icon name. For icon_source: 'official', one of
    format/hair_type/technology/ingredients/how_to/interest_data (see
    montibello-luxlight-icon.liquid). Otherwise an icon.liquid name.
  @param {string} [icon_source] - 'official' or omitted (theme icons, default)
  @param {string} [arrow] - official disclosure marker: 'chevron_right' (default) or 'arrow_long'
{% enddoc %}

<details class="montibello-pdp-accordion-item{% if icon_source == 'official' %} montibello-pdp-accordion-item--official{% endif %}" data-montibello-accordion>
  <summary class="montibello-pdp-accordion-item__label">
    <span class="montibello-pdp-accordion-item__icon-left" aria-hidden="true">
      {% if icon_source == 'official' %}
        {% render 'montibello-luxlight-icon', icon: icon %}
      {% else %}
        <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
          {% render 'icon', icon: icon %}
        </svg>
      {% endif %}
    </span>
    <span class="montibello-pdp-accordion-item__text">{{ label }}</span>
    <span class="montibello-pdp-accordion-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">
      {% if icon_source == 'official' %}
        {% assign arrow_icon = arrow | default: 'chevron_right' %}
        {% render 'montibello-luxlight-icon', icon: arrow_icon %}
      {% else %}
        <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
          {% render 'icon', icon: 'arrow' %}
        </svg>
      {% endif %}
    </span>
  </summary>
  <div class="montibello-pdp-accordion-item__content" data-montibello-accordion-content>{{ content }}</div>
</details>

{%- comment -%}
  Styling AND the smooth-expand JS for `.montibello-pdp-accordion-item*`
  both live in montibello-product-main.liquid (the only current renderer of
  this snippet) — `{% stylesheet %}`/`{% javascript %}` tags are only valid
  in section/block files, not snippets, and Shopify dedupes a section's own
  javascript/stylesheet output automatically regardless of how many times
  the section (or a snippet it renders) appears on the page.
{%- endcomment -%}
